+.. rst:directive:: .. py:type:: name
+
+   Describes a type alias. The alias may be declared at module level or inside
+   a class. The optional :rst:directive:option:`canonical` option gives the
+   alias expression; its type names are parsed as Python cross-references.
+   Type aliases can contain a description body, but do not establish a nested
+   namespace.
+
+   .. rubric:: options
+
+   .. rst:directive:option:: canonical
+      :type: type expression
+
+      Describe the expression assigned to the type alias.
+
+   .. rst:directive:option:: module
+      :type: text
+
+      Describe the location where the object is defined. The default value is
+      the module specified by :rst:dir:`py:currentmodule`.
+
